          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "A career after a PhD in biotechnology can go to academia, industry research and development, regulatory affairs, medical writing, technology transfer or a startup, and planning early with a transferable skills list and a network outside your lab makes the move far easier."
          },
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "List the skills your PhD built, speak to people in two target paths and publish or document one project that shows applied value."
          },
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Check official notices and avoid paying agents for positions."
          }
        ]
      },
